<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anglo-Soviet invasion of Iran</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1941">1941</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Anglo-Soviet invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> took place in August and September 1941, when British and Soviet forces occupied the country to secure its oilfields and a supply route to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reza-shah">Reza Shah</a>, suspected of German sympathies, was forced to abdicate in favour of his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohammad-reza-pahlavi">Mohammad Reza Shah</a>, and Iran remained occupied until 1946.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anglo-soviet-invasion-of-iran.jpg" alt="Anglo-Soviet invasion of Iran" width="320" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Soviet_tankmen_of_the_6th_Armoured_Division_drive_through_the_streets_of_Tabriz_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
